[01:18:12] [INFO] [step_11_eht_polarization]    TEP Exterior-Null Analysis
[01:18:12] [INFO] [step_11_eht_polarization] ================================================================================
[01:18:12] [INFO] [step_11_eht_polarization] 
[01:18:12] [INFO] [step_11_eht_polarization]   Under TEP, the conformal factor A(phi) = exp(beta_A * phi)
[01:18:12] [INFO] [step_11_eht_polarization]   and the bounded disformal function B(phi) govern the coupling
[01:18:12] [INFO] [step_11_eht_polarization]   between the scalar field and the EM field.
[01:18:12] [INFO] [step_11_eht_polarization] 
[01:18:12] [INFO] [step_11_eht_polarization]   In the exterior (weak field, phi -> 0):
[01:18:12] [INFO] [step_11_eht_polarization]     A(phi) ~ exp(beta_A * phi) -> 1
[01:18:12] [INFO] [step_11_eht_polarization]     B(phi) ~ B0 * |phi|^n -> 0
[01:18:12] [INFO] [step_11_eht_polarization]   The disformal coupling B * (dphi/dr)^2 vanishes in the exterior,
[01:18:12] [INFO] [step_11_eht_polarization]   so there is no birefringence: both polarization modes propagate
[01:18:12] [INFO] [step_11_eht_polarization]   with the same phase velocity. Photon polarization is unaffected.
[01:18:12] [INFO] [step_11_eht_polarization] 
[01:18:12] [INFO] [step_11_eht_polarization]   The disformal term only matters inside the horizon, where
[01:18:12] [INFO] [step_11_eht_polarization]   phi grows large in magnitude and B -> B0. Photons observed by the EHT
[01:18:12] [INFO] [step_11_eht_polarization]   escape from the exterior (r > r_h), so any interior disformal
[01:18:12] [INFO] [step_11_eht_polarization]   effect is not imprinted on the observed polarization signal.
[01:18:12] [INFO] [step_11_eht_polarization] 
[01:18:12] [INFO] [step_11_eht_polarization] 
[01:18:12] [INFO] [step_11_eht_polarization] 
